  "backstory": "Born in 1990 in Guatemala City, GTM. As he prepares for fatherhood in the small town in Departamento de Guatemala, this 29-year-old man embodies a blend of ambition and anxiety. He is driven by a desire to succeed, believing that external achievements will validate his worth, yet he grapples with an internal struggle\u2014his own feelings often suppressed in favor of societal expectations. In relationships, he projects warmth to those close to him, yet maintains an air of authority that can create distance, fearing that vulnerability might expose him to judgment. His hope rests on providing a better life for his child, fueled by a strong sense of duty, yet he worries deeply that he may not be able to express the unconditional love he feels, having never fully received it himself. As he prepares his home and heart for the arrival of his baby, he wrestles with the unspoken belief that feelings are a weakness, convinced that to be a \"good father\" he must prioritize stability and success over emotional connection. Ultimately, he stands at a crossroads, hoping to break the cycle of disconnection, yet unsure how to embrace the tender, messy reality of parenthood. In the quiet town in Departamento de Guatemala, a 23-year-old mother-to-be navigates the whirlwind of impending motherhood with a mix of trepidation and determination. As a Type 5 Enneagram, she often retreats into the sanctuary of her thoughts, fearing the chaos of the outside world and believing that vulnerability is a luxury she cannot afford. Her warm heart is marred by an underlying belief that her needs are burdensome; she struggles to reconcile her aspirations for a nurturing environment with her instinct to maintain emotional distance. Her parenting style, though rooted in authority, often feels like a tightrope walk between the desire to protect and the fear of being too involved, leaving her hesitant to fully embrace the joy of the moment. \n\nWith the backdrop of a rapidly changing Gu